guard 1.0.0

Checks and repairs a project against the policies in its guard.yaml. Running guard without a command runs check.

Usage:
  command [options] [arguments]

Options:
  -h, --help            Display help for the given command, or list the commands when none is given
      --silent          Do not output any message
  -q, --quiet           Only errors are displayed. All other output is suppressed
  -V, --version         Display this application version
      --ansi|--no-ansi  Force (or disable --no-ansi) ANSI output
  -n, --no-interaction  Do not ask any interactive question
  -v|vv|vvv, --verbose  Increase the verbosity of messages: 1 for normal output, 2 for more verbose output and 3 for debug

Available commands:
  apply       Repair the violations guard can fix, then report what remains
  check       Check the project against its policy without changing any file
  completion  Dump the shell completion script
  help        Display help for a command
  init        Create a policy file with the presets that fit the project
  list        List commands
  -c, --config=CONFIG   Policy file, relative to the working directory [default: "guard.yaml"]
      --import=IMPORT   Import only these presets, comma-separated or repeated, instead of detecting them (multiple values allowed)
  -h, --help            Display help for the given command, or list the commands when none is given
      --silent          Do not output any message
  -q, --quiet           Only errors are displayed. All other output is suppressed
  -V, --version         Display this application version
      --ansi|--no-ansi  Force (or disable --no-ansi) ANSI output
  -n, --no-interaction  Do not ask any interactive question
  -v|vv|vvv, --verbose  Increase the verbosity of messages: 1 for normal output, 2 for more verbose output and 3 for debug

Help:
  Writes a policy file for the project and refuses to overwrite one that
  exists. Without --import, the presets are selected from the tools and
  documents the project has; --import names them instead.

  Presets: metrics, structure, disable-doc, phpstan, phpstan-guard-rules, phpunit9, phpunit10, phpunit11, phpunit12, phpunit13, doctest9, doctest10, doctest11, doctest12, doctest13, php-cs-fixer, phpcs, deptrac, infection, composer, github-actions, mutation, pbt, fuzz, phpbench, docgen, agents-md, claude-md, readme-md

  Exit codes:
    0  policy file created
    2  invalid command line, existing policy file or unknown preset
